03" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{1}{3}m+\\frac{2}{3}n"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6c073ab64f52cb58db0936f6c454f3e079fc66b4306dea36c57aafb21a7b489" "basis" 1641 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-367064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/assets/80cedeceb8d377617af880cab1c383643e3cd79055eccce046b0418598897ac8.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $c=\\lambda a-2b,$ then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6c073ab64f52cb58db0936f6c454f3e079fc66b4306dea36c57aafb21a7b489" "basis" 1641 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-367064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a-2b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $-2b.$ So, we first draw the vector $-2b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/assets/7e6923e8b8b774eeaa2f885ec6aa24bb03f07c547fa50e7145a4113a18e92e8a.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $-2b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=2|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-2a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =-2b-2a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a-2b=-2a-2b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-2\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6c073ab64f52cb58db0936f6c454f3e079fc66b4306dea36c57aafb21a7b489" "basis" 1641 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-367064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4f3ea802dd0f66ca870281a32fee5a331d99d3806c48f8a1e76495e29627d6a4" "basis" 1641 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-367064" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6c073ab64f52cb58db0936f6c454f3e079fc66b4306dea36c57aafb21a7b489" "basis" 1641 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-367064" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "d6c073ab64f52cb58db0936f6c454f3e079fc66b4306dea36c57aa