rse_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/state.json" "file_sha256" "92811f893e9927ae1b3f76b695d45a2fb034849d678ce43fe03026bd62f1ff5a" "basis" 2611 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-325974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "11c191ae8e2641d8e32dc83a684af92f102dca348edd2c027c4163fe1ba2fdfb" "basis" 2611 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-325974" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/state.json" "file_sha256" "92811f893e9927ae1b3f76b695d45a2fb034849d678ce43fe03026bd62f1ff5a" "basis" 2611 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-19338" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/816c4ecbfe49321bc6b2bc0d72eb61d6ddd1aeae7e76a275df0975439dde5865.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=a+\\lambda b,$ find $\\lambda .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/state.json" "file_sha256" "c08025d4a49cc2cdf60b64859cbb3b2f43dcee6ee8e3852b1acaabc7b0947d6e"} {"question" "q-19338" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=a+\\lambda b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $a.$ So, we begin with the vector $a,$ and then find the remaining vector needed to reach the point $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/6782f2fa59056afd9022edbaf69c44a991bf12a7ac6a190bea3cc08fc7a4996c.png)\n\nNote that in $△OAC,$ we have:\n\n- $AC=2.5|b|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $b$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=2.5b.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =a+2.5b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=a+\\lambda b=a+2.5b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $b,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =2.5\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/state.json" "file_sha256" "c08025d4a49cc2cdf60b64859cbb3b2f43dcee6ee8e3852b1acaabc7b0947d6e"} {"question" "q-19338" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0357189807dde4a8c521cd09a69f210f341a5cfd8c7709433377b3ffa5416436"} {"question" "q-19338" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/state.json" "file_sha256" "c08025d4a49cc2cdf60b64859cbb3b2f43dcee6ee8e3852b1acaabc7b0947d6e"} {"question" "q-19338" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "2.5"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/state.json" "file_sha256" "c08025d4a49cc2cdf60b64859cbb3b2f43dcee6ee8e3852b1acaabc7b