\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=3|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-3a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =2b-3a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a+2b=-3a+2b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-3\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/state.json" "file_sha256" "c08025d4a49cc2cdf60b64859cbb3b2f43dcee6ee8e3852b1acaabc7b0947d6e"} {"question" "q-367061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0357189807dde4a8c521cd09a69f210f341a5cfd8c7709433377b3ffa5416436"} {"question" "q-367061" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/state.json" "file_sha256" "c08025d4a49cc2cdf60b64859cbb3b2f43dcee6ee8e3852b1acaabc7b0947d6e"} {"question" "q-367061" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/state.json" "file_sha256" "c08025d4a49cc2cdf60b64859cbb3b2f43dcee6ee8e3852b1acaabc7b0947d6e"} {"question" "q-367064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/80cedeceb8d377617af880cab1c383643e3cd79055eccce046b0418598897ac8.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $c=\\lambda a-2b,$ then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma