oper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/state.json" "file_sha256" "c08025d4a49cc2cdf60b64859cbb3b2f43dcee6ee8e3852b1acaabc7b0947d6e"} {"question" "q-322575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OR}=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OP}=p,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{PR}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OPQ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{PO}+\\overset{\\to }{OQ} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{OQ} \\\\  & =-p+q \\\\  & =q-p.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $PR:RQ=4:9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{PR}=\\frac{4}{13}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=\\frac{4}{13}(q-p).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OR} & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\  & =p+\\frac{4}{13}(q-p) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{13}p+\\frac{4}{13}q.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/state.json" "file_sha256" "c08025d4a49cc2cdf60b64859cbb3b2f43dcee6ee8e3852b1acaabc7b0947d6e"} {"question" "q-322575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0357189807dde4a8c521cd09a69f210f341a5cfd8c7709433377b3ffa5416436"} {"question" "q-322575" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/state.json" "file_sha256" "c08025d4a49cc2cdf60b64859cbb3b2f43dcee6ee8e3852b1acaabc7b0947d6e"} {"question" "q-322575" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{13}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/state.json" "file_sha256" "c08025d4a49cc2cdf60b64859cbb3b2f43dcee6ee8e3852b1acaabc7b0947d6e"} {"question" "q-322575" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/state.json" "file_sha256" "c08025d4a49cc2cdf60b64859cbb3b2f43dcee6ee8e3852b1acaabc7b0947d6e"} {"question" "q-322575" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{13}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/state.json" "file_sha256" "c08025d4a49cc2cdf60b64859cbb3b2f43dcee6ee8e3852b1acaabc7b0947d6e"} {"question" "e-5212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the picture below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/f2518c2e998e7c7f551548a4cc7283720a66428ea8fa9872494a81cc3848ba9e.png)\n\nGiven that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/c6714d0a6eaa5c7d354d46e8d6d60da7f3d2011df0fc75773036cf7ae510c5e3.png), find ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/24878591902884f45f14f5c447bc326586a411a8870b205fc12825a4ab2c738a.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/example-5212.json" "file_sha256" "1f5ec1f01f4cb4af010730c535b2790310ac2591757c866bbefb0e635401c223"} {"question" "e-5212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when two known vectors are not parallel, a linear combination of them is unique. So, once we rewrite ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/5c644b15efcf5a4274de23242a722604ead2ff800ea29ba7a650729227fefdf0.png) in terms of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/27f36b1d1846e12e3c50b7d4e47f5745727792d52a48e4d85b689ec36e3d25a0.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/a7b9033c421072576aaf959980d778c319a8ed0f849e08db644b63bc6994088c.png) we can match coefficients to determine the unknown scalar.\n\nTo find ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/166c90a9c29f99347bff6b397f31d705ec6407a19b4d71246f98308bbd7a5473.png) we want to match the expression\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/fc79367916dd7671c17de4f40b3d83f91d41c2f9988645964de0b53e5b11ab9b.png)\n\nWe are given that one of the components is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/91f686c6ca02e85c386cb0f9e80b66beface446d3a541952e0ac91738ad0db37.png) So, we first draw the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/d54b9a8919c7b6106fcf5770c62b1823605d7be98a55d5333e73bcfb7528997a.png) from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/6e1bbbe9eb66856824ff70d16cc2c077519d361546b226a67146e20f15a24dd0.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/ea517ac4ca8e0bcf7ba48f23e66f100323d5485f1221219aacfbea9148f4a1af.png)\n\nNote that in ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/f1c944e6afa4e9cd84bc68004a2bfd918d81498a727aeb7c56ec627806bf93f6.png), we have:\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/b7ac390c4e43b2fa2fbb4063632f98869256cea877caa5e5dad4aad33ae94722.png)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/7e5f2b01647ab01052fff18ab760273eebe19d47b56051b1953adf587d7f9fb3.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/784225d11bf94b7fbd67f8e2395695141eb75b1cb44f89d49b29bb3a2031534b.png) have the same direction\n\nHence, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/21261c8ad0d86a9e7300ffc58c57fd76beef9f627492bcfe2051d5e3cfd82a4e.png)\n\nAdditionally,\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/ae9c98ded3aa4317a729571710ad38d973a2d67b5faeb9ad26af7c24ee5c3193.png)\n\nConsequently, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/aee3287ad64a654880216142756811bd4d5232b3dba2f48378b8b1c5241e4316.png)\n\nSince ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/466863f8c7522ac89896a4233a823be02940535097c28328fa2c9e9e1f4bc3d8.png) the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/3720c5887713d3f7a29be384fe5e883390935b2b9b469af626a8dba968f4da8b.png) we get:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/4ac145b710c5354b44a4ea1dc820d70f54b5c17985f078fce6313b671ec26fd9.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/example-5212.json" "file_sha256" "1f5ec1f01f4cb4af010730c535b2790310ac2591757c866bbefb0e635401c223"} {"question" "e-26144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the picture below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073957/assets/d4f18c3567d0c55d3d6e002fbe2c6ac50b97b7adc14b016c8e95006de98ca15d.png)\n\nGiven that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/referen