}$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overrightarrow{NM}=2\\mathbf{k}$.\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\overset{\\to }{ON}+\\overset{\\to }{NM} \\\\  & =2n+2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $\\mathbf{m}=\\lambda\\mathbf{n}+\\mu\\mathbf{k}=2\\mathbf{n}+2\\mathbf{k}$. \n\nSince $\\mathbf{n} \\nparallel \\mathbf{k},$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $\\mathbf{n}$ and $\\mathbf{k}$, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda=2$ and $\\mu=2$"] [17592186096375 :question/problem "Consider the following diagram, where $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b},$ and $X$ divides $AB$ in the ratio $3:1.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{OX}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/assets/678ea2936b8a5b1ded74cb8a0875c629e8be0f7002c98492ebf2e8109fc603ef.png)"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186094893 17592186094894 17592186094895 17592186094896 17592186094897 17592186095001 17592186095002 17592186095003 17592186095004 17592186095005 17592186310723 17592186310724 17592186310725 17592186310726 17592186310727 17592186310730 17592186310731 17592186310732 17592186310733 17592186310734 17592186310744 17592186310760 17592186310761 17592186310763 17592186322254 17592186322255 17592186322256 17592186322257 17592186322258 17592186322261 17592186322262 17592186322263 17592186322264 17592186322265 17592186322274 17592186374586 17592186374587] "immutable_fields" [[17592186094892 :answer-field/correct] [17592186094892 :answer-field/id] [17592186094892 :answer-field/key] [17592186094892 :answer-field/type] [17592186095000 :answer-field/correct] [17592186095000 :answer-field/id] [17592186095000 :answer-field/key] [17592186095000 :answer-field/type] [17592186310722 :answer-field/correct] [17592186310722 :answer-field/id] [17592186310722 :answer-field/key] [17592186310722 :answer-field/type] [17592186310729 :answer-field/correct] [17592186310729 :answer-field/id] 